{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112868","id":3015830950,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6zwe2m","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112868","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112868.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112868.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112868","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112868/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112868/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112868/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d0447da44f0b14d466d1af23c29f5e52a5817fa4","number":112868,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Explain how `@export_group` can be nested just like subgroups","user":{"login":"Yobbolita","id":198503602,"node_id":"U_kgDOC9Tssg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198503602?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita","html_url":"https://github.com/Yobbolita","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Yobbolita/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The GdScript docs say that @export_groups cannot be nested, but `@export_subgroups` can be nested with /\r\n\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40gdscript.html#class-gdscript-annotation-export-group\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40gdscript.html#class-gdscript-annotation-export-subgroup\r\n\r\nThat's, like, not true. You can nest using / with both groups and subgroups.\r\n\r\nHere is an example using the code from the docs, but I swapped \"subgroup\" with \"group\" :\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1379\" height=\"326\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28abfc30-5207-4267-b72f-e2baeff6ad99\" />\r\n\r\nSo I fixed the docs to reflect this.\r\n\r\nHowever, this does put into question why we even have both `@export_group` and `@export_subgroup` if they do the same thing.\r\n\r\n------------------------------------------\r\n\r\nAlso, I don't get why we are told to go on the godot-docs repo for issues, only to then be sent back here \r\n<img width=\"879\" height=\"251\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2297fc3-3fa9-4115-a3c0-7fba0f1e0ef1\" />\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"","color":"ffddff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-